Briar Midwife — full-art + animation kit

Approved D3 identity: ivory faceplate and horizontal slit, flared woven-willow collar, interlaced torso and slender legs, two broad hooked thorn hands, teal draped cloth. Native 1024×1536 full-art master with genuine alpha; no engine changes.

Runtime: all frames RGBA 768×768. Pivot (350,660) px from top-left, normalized (0.4557291667,0.859375). +x right, +y down. Three-quarter facing screen-right. Root motion is in-place. Use JSON per-frame durations, not a guessed global frame rate. The 3072×3072 atlases have 4×4 cells; use each JSON atlas rectangle. Do not auto-trim frames or recenter each silhouette.

Eight clips: idle, move, strike, special, hit, defeat, spawn, snarefx. Character clips have 12 evolving generated cels plus canonical or loop endpoints when needed (defeat:12; others:13). Effects have 12 evolving cels plus an empty endpoint. Animation is pose-drawn, not scale/fade-only. Sources have four cels per native 1024×1536 page; runtime uses downsampling and registration only. Source provenance and actual scale are supplied per frame. Endpoint cels are explicitly marked.

Attack timing: strike and special each have 1040ms readable anticipation, a 55ms committed impact cel, follow-through and recovery. Each has one event at 1040ms (frame index6). Consume the event once per play; do not apply repeated hits during a hold. Target center is +280px horizontally from actor pivot; ground footprint ellipse radii95×45. Strike collision volume can extend from ground up to490px; the forward hand travels through this target column. Radius/height are integration guidance, not engine code.

Special: start separate snarefx at760ms, offset(+280,0) from actor pivot. Its cage closes at effect280ms, exactly1040ms on the cast timeline. The effect event is visual-only: special owns the single gameplay bind. Keep the same world-space target position for the complete effect, even after the actor moves. Consumer chooses gameplay bind duration.

Loop endpoints duplicate first contact/ready for safe transitions; if your animator automatically repeats the first cel at wrap, omit the terminal endpoint hold to avoid a double dwell. Defeat ends on a held fallen pose. Spawn and hit return to canonical ready. Preview ground lines, pivot dots, labels and target rings are diagnostic overlays only, never part of the RGBA assets.

One ZIP per clip includes frames, atlas, JSON, the three selected native source pages, source prompts, contact sheet and MP4. No redundant whole-collection ZIP. The original approved concept and revised unused sources are retained locally for traceability but are not redundant uploads. Built-in imagegen was used for every art drawing.
